    "# Week 8 — Gradient Boosting II: LightGBM + SHAP + Model Stacking\n",
    "**Date:** July 28, 2026\n",
    "**Week:** 8 of 10 — follows Week 7 (XGBoost, closed out; SHAP explicitly deferred to this week)\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost edged out RF as your best single model this week just closed, but by a thin margin, and RF's two weak spots (`class_target_2`, `class_target_3_corrected` LONG) got closed rather than blown open — worth keeping in mind before this week's tools invite overconfidence. This week has four real jobs, in order: (1) finally compile the RF-vs-XGBoost win/loss tally Week 7 never assembled, so \"current best\" means something concrete; (2) add LightGBM as a third tree ensemble and run SHAP across all three models together — the interpretability pass Week 7 deliberately postponed rather than redoing later; (3) build a stacking ensemble to see whether combining model families beats any single one; (4) do a genuine mid-point review of every model trained since Week 1, plus a first look at regime-dependence (trending vs ranging markets). None of this is a free pass to treat this week's numbers as more solid than last week's — SHAP agreement, stacking gains, and regime splits are all new places for optimistic bias to hide if you don't check for it the same way you checked Week 4's `class_target_3`.\n"
